Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||03-16-2000||08:51 AM||||I am planning on putting an SE nose on my GT (so that I can drive it) until I can find a GT nose.  The mold (the one that lines up with the side marker lights) is not the same rounded shape (at least the one that I have) and can be notice if you are looking for it, but for a daily commuter and for the current need for the car I am going to do this.<P>They should bolt right up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-16-2000||10:49 AM||||Yes they will bolt up with no problem. As for the molding, The SE nose piece for the point of the molding is seperate from the nose and ribbed. On the GT it is molded as part of the front end. But all other molding will fit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||03-16-2000||11:10 PM||||So wait... does this mean I can NOT change those little 2" pieces of molding on an SE nose to the rounded shape?  I am putting thise nose on so I can get the car painted, so obviously I don't want to be stuck with mis-matching trim.  If I remember correctly, the trim on my GT nose looked like it could be removed.  I can get a pretty good deal on an SE nose here, so if I can MAKE it work, I will.  Does the great Ogre have anything to say about this?||||reg||1
